    "## Step 1: Download the raw telescope data\n",
    "\n",
    "Before we can do anything, we need the actual image. This comes from the\n",
    "James Webb Space Telescope's NIRCam instrument, as part of the COSMOS-Web\n",
    "survey (a large-area imaging program). MAST (the Mikulski Archive for Space\n",
    "Telescopes) is NASA's public archive -- anyone can query and download this\n",
    "data, which is part of why strong lensing research is so reproducible.\n"
   ]
